1. VERIFY BRANCH. 2. Comment on GitHub Issue with plan: mcp__github__add_issue_comment — "## Planned

```xml
{plan.xml}
```" 3. Create Draft PR: mcp__github__create_pull_request (title: "{title}", head: {github-branch}, base: main, draft: true, body: "Closes #{issueNumber}

_Draft — not yet implemented._") 4. Add github-pr="#{N}" to task.xml.

1. Verify on main. If not, error and exit. 2. Create GitHub Issue: mcp__github__create_issue (title, body, labels: ["quick"], assignees). Add github-issue="#N" to quick.xml. 3. Create branch and push: git checkout -b quick/{id} (error if exists). Add github-branch="quick/{id}" to quick.xml. git push -u origin quick/{id} 4. Commit code: git add {files} && git commit -m "quick(#{issueNumber}): {title}" 5. If docs updated: git add .festinalente/product/ .festinalente/engineering/ && git commit --amend --no-edit 6. git push 7. Create PR: mcp__github__create_pull_request (title: "quick(#{issueNumber}): {title}", head: quick/{id}, base: main, body: "Closes #{issueNumber}

## Summary
{brief description}"). Add github-pr="#{N}" to quick.xml. Ask: "Merge now or wait for review?" Merge: mcp__github__merge_pull_request (merge_method: "squash"). git checkout main && git fetch origin && git reset --hard origin/main && git branch -D quick/{id} Wait: EXIT.
